# Mulsetu folder structure

Write every application file inside `mulsetu/` only. Do not create source files at the workspace root or in any other directory.

```
mulsetu/
├── app/                    # Next.js App Router pages only
├── components/
│   ├── layout/             # Navbar, Footer, page chrome
│   ├── ui/                 # Button, Badge, Card, SectionHeading, primitives
│   ├── home/               # Home page sections
│   ├── services/           # Service page sections
│   └── pages/              # Other page sections (our-work, products, about, blog)
├── data/                   # services.ts, projects.ts, products.ts, navigation.ts
├── lib/                    # helpers and utilities
├── public/                 # images/, logos/, icons/
├── styles/                 # global CSS
└── docs/                   # design-system.md and design notes
```

## Placement

- Routes → `mulsetu/app/.../page.tsx`
- Navbar / Footer → `mulsetu/components/layout/`
- Reusable UI → `mulsetu/components/ui/`
- Home sections → `mulsetu/components/home/`
- Service sections → `mulsetu/components/services/`
- Other page sections → `mulsetu/components/pages/`
- Content arrays / types → `mulsetu/data/`
- Helpers → `mulsetu/lib/`
- Assets → `mulsetu/public/`
- Global styles → `mulsetu/styles/`
- Design tokens / notes → `mulsetu/docs/`

## Do not

- Put components next to pages
- Add a second `components/`, `src/`, or `app/` outside `mulsetu/`
- Invent folders that are not in this tree
